  "body": "### Problem or current behavior\n\nThe viewer interprets model output as markdown, math, links, media, syntax highlighting, and terminal output. Researchers evaluating models they do not trust need a way to inspect those payloads as literal text, including existing logs whose tasks did not opt out of rich rendering.\n\n### Result or new behavior\n\nTasks can set `ViewerConfig(trust_content=False)`. The viewer then displays the log's payloads plainly, reveals hidden/bidi characters, shows terminal escape sequences literally, and substitutes placeholders for media. JSON-shaped strings and tool output retain their original content instead of passing through optional formatting.\n\n```python\nTask(..., viewer=ViewerConfig(trust_content=False))\n```\n\nAn app-wide ceiling applies to every log, including existing ones:\n\n- `inspect view` / `inspect view start --no-trust-content`, or `INSPECT_VIEW_TRUST_CONTENT=false`.\n- `inspect view bundle` / `inspect view embed --no-trust-content`.\n- Python `view()`, `bundle_log_dir()`, and `embed_log_dir()` accept `trust_content=`.\n\nThe task ceiling cannot raise the app ceiling. The setting is forwarded through `/app-config` or a bundle's `log_dir_context`, including options supplied before a subcommand. Retries preserve an existing `trust_content=False` while retaining other viewer settings from the reloaded task.\n\nThe paired [meridianlabs-ai/ts-mono#713](https://github.com/meridianlabs-ai/ts-mono/pull/713) implements intersected rendering permissions, early plain dispatch, separate application cells, and policy-aware rich renderers. This PR includes its published commit `6f8008d6` and the rebuilt viewer bundle. Documentation includes task marking with `task_with()` and both ceilings.\n\n### Compatibility and migration\n\nNo migration required. Existing logs and configurations without either setting retain their default rendering.\n\n- Task producers (`Task`, `task_with`, eval and retry) record optional `ViewerConfig.trust_content` in `EvalSpec.viewer`. Log readers/writers and the generated OpenAPI/TypeScript types preserve it. The viewer uses the header belonging to the displayed content's source; loading headers are plain. Absent/null/true retain the legacy default, while false and unrecognized values restrict rendering.\n- Viewer launchers and CLI commands send optional `AppConfig.trust_content` through `/app-config`; the served viewer and VS Code proxy consume it. Bundlers/embedders store it in `index.html` via `log_dir_context`. Scout does not yet honor task markings.\n- Older viewers ignore the field. Older Inspect versions may drop it when rewriting a log. Re-bundling/re-embedding without the option, including `eval_set(embed_viewer=True)`, removes the embedded app ceiling. These limits are documented.\n- Trust is assumed stable for a log identity. Replacing a file in place with a differently marked log is outside this feature's contract.\n\n### Validation\n\nTask marking round-trips through real `.eval` files, retries retain it, and CLI/server/bundle tests cover option forwarding and both ceilings. The paired viewer's final feature suite passes 42 browser tests, with another 33 checks passing against its production build.\n\nLocal runs on macOS, Python 3.12.13, at this bundle/pin update (base main `674e62823`):\n\n- `make check`: passed.\n- `PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" PYTEST_ADDOPTS=\"-n 4\" make test`: 14,242 passed, 6,900 skipped.\n- The exact changelog gate passes; both entries remain under Unreleased.\n- Schema and TypeScript regeneration against the paired branch is a no-op. Two independent viewer builds match all 25 shipped bundle files.\n- Bundle/embed gated tests and the view-server Trio tests pass; commands and counts are below.\n- The broader local TypeScript browser run had one navigation failure that reproduces on its clean current main. Current-head Linux CI passed all 210 browser tests; the paired PR reports the baseline comparison.\n\n### Slow tests\n\n- Bundle/embed, macOS/Python 3.12.13: `.venv/bin/pytest --runslow tests/view/test_bundle.py -q` — 9 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped.\n- View server, macOS/Python 3.12.13: `.venv/bin/pytest --runtrio tests/_view/test_view_server.py -q` — 14 passed, 0 failed, 148 skipped (tests outside the Trio-only selection).\n- Not run: Docker sandbox and live model-provider classes; this feature changes viewer configuration/rendering and does not change those subsystems.\n\n### Agent review\n\n- Viewer cleanup: one further independent Codex/GPT-6 review pass in a fresh context found no actionable issues. This update only refreshes the embedded bundle and published TypeScript pin; it changes no Python source. Bundle/embed tests were rerun against the rebuilt viewer.\n\n- This update: Codex (GPT-6), including the coordinated bundle/pin and current-main merge. The paired UI refactor received one fresh-context Codex/GPT-6 subagent review plus follow-up verification: eight initial finding groups and three follow-up edges, all fixed; final verification found no remaining actionable issue. No findings were dismissed. This update makes no further Python source changes.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prior author-disclosed reviews</summary>\n\n\n- Authoring: Claude Code (Claude Opus 5.5).\n- UI half (meridianlabs-ai/ts-mono#713): a fresh-context adversarial security review (Claude Opus 5.5 subagent, 1 pass) found 3 issues, all fixed. A later automated review of meridianlabs-ai/ts-mono#713 left 2 suggestions, both fixed.\n- This PR's Python diff: a fresh-context review (Claude Opus 5.5 subagent, 1 pass) found 4 issues, all fixed:\n  - **`eval_retry` dropped `trust_content=False` when it was set with `task_with()`**, the method the docs recommend. The retry reloads the task from its definition, while the retried log carries the untrusted samples over. A retry now keeps the previous log's `trust_content=False` and preserves the reloaded task's other viewer settings. Covered by 2 new tests in `tests/test_retry.py`.\n  - The docs' `task_with()` example now keeps a task's existing viewer settings.\n  - The field docstring now describes all the behavior: media, links and hidden characters.\n  - `Task`/`task_with` had a stale `viewer` docstring, now updated.\n- The viewer-wide option (both repos): a fresh-context review (Claude Opus 5.5 subagent, 1 pass) found 6 issues:\n  - **Fixed:** `inspect view --no-trust-content bundle` silently dropped the setting, because the `view` group ignores its own options when a subcommand runs. It's now forwarded to the subcommand, with tests.\n  - **Documented:** re-embedding, including `eval_set(embed_viewer=True)`, drops the setting.\n  - **Fixed:** the new CLI tests were in a new file; they're now in the existing `tests/_cli/test_view.py`.\n  - **Fixed:** added tests for rejecting invalid environment values and for bundle/embed writing the setting into `index.html`.\n  - **Fixed:** the CHANGELOG and help wording.\n  - **Initially deferred:** the viewer bundle and gitlink are now included and pin the published TypeScript branch, as described above.\n\n\n</details>\n\n### Coordination\n\nThis branch is pinned to the published TypeScript PR head. `submodule-on-main` is expected to fail until [ts-mono#713](https://github.com/meridianlabs-ai/ts-mono/pull/713) is merged. Review both PRs before merging TypeScript; after a squash/rebase merge, update this gitlink and rebuild from the merged commit before landing this PR.\n",
